{"documentCount":34,"nextId":34,"documentIds":{"0":"faq/","1":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions","2":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions-do-i-need-to-pay-to-use-youtube","3":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions-slowbroken-yt-loadingdownloads","4":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions-lyrics-source","5":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions-change-lyrics-source","6":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions-is-there-a-lastfm-scrobble-feature","7":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions-is-there-a-discord-rich-presence-feature-rpc","8":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions-equalizer-issues-or-missing-feature","9":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions-spotify-support","10":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions-some-flac-files-have-no-sound-at-some-point","11":"/","12":"/#quick-start-your-docs","13":"/#quick-start-your-docs-run-the-dev-server","14":"/#quick-start-your-docs-build-for-production","15":"/#quick-start-your-docs-project-structure","16":"/#quick-start-your-docs-features","17":"/#quick-start-your-docs-features-1-smart-containers","18":"/#quick-start-your-docs-features-2-tabs-and-code","19":"/#quick-start-your-docs-features-3-built-in-plugins","20":"/#quick-start-your-docs-next-steps","21":"settings/1-theme-settings/","22":"settings/2-indexer-settings/","23":"settings/","24":"settings/#settings","25":"skills/","26":"skills/#agent-skills","27":"skills/#agent-skills-what-gets-installed","28":"skills/#agent-skills-install","29":"skills/#agent-skills-install-claude-code","30":"skills/#agent-skills-install-cursor","31":"skills/#agent-skills-install-project-local-any-agent","32":"skills/#agent-skills-how-it-works-at-runtime","33":"skills/#agent-skills-update-or-remove"},"fieldIds":{"title":0,"headings":1,"text":2},"fieldLength":{"0":[1,43,288],"1":[5,3,1],"2":[10,8,1],"3":[7,5,1],"4":[4,2,1],"5":[5,3,1],"6":[9,7,1],"7":[11,9,1],"8":[7,5,1],"9":[4,2,1],"10":[11,9,1],"11":[2,28,194],"12":[6,5,1],"13":[7,4,1],"14":[6,3,1],"15":[5,2,1],"16":[4,1,1],"17":[6,3,1],"18":[7,4,1],"19":[7,4,1],"20":[5,2,1],"21":[2,1,5],"22":[2,1,1],"23":[1,1,27],"24":[2,1,1],"25":[2,21,162],"26":[3,2,1],"27":[6,3,1],"28":[4,1,1],"29":[5,2,1],"30":[4,1,1],"31":[8,5,1],"32":[8,5,1],"33":[6,3,1]},"averageFieldLength":[5.352941176470588,5.852941176470588,20.735294117647058],"storedFields":{"0":{"title":"FAQ","id":"faq/","text":"Frequently Asked Questions\nDo I need to pay to use youtube?\n\nNot really, searching, playing videos, liking or downloading, seeing your playlists (and many others) is totally free.\ngetting a membership means u access newly added yt features (beside supporting), these features only make sense when you are logged in your yt account.\nyou can get a membership throught patreon on https://patreon.com/namidaco\nif you have donated throught kofi or buymeacoffee, you should get a coupon on ur email, altho not instant as patreon and may take more than few days\nyou can log in from Settings -&gt; Youtube -&gt; Manage your accounts -&gt; Add account to access your playlists and like videos/etc.\nfor more info about these features https://www.patreon.com/posts/namida-yt-112913142\n\nSlow/Broken yt loading/downloads\nThis can happen frequently when youtube pushes updates that break clients.\nMost yt issues are fixed asap in beta, try latest beta from here https://github.com/namidaco/namida-snapshots/releases\nLyrics Source\nhttps://lrclib.net/\nChange Lyrics Source\n\nnot possible directly\nyou can select the LRC file (by long pressing lyrics icon in miniplayer -&gt; add) or just edit tags and paste the lyrics in the lyrics section\nyou can also copy the LRC file and put it in the same directory as the song, it will appear as long as the filename is the same as the song\nmake sure “Prioritize embedded lyrics” is enabled/disabled depending on where u put the lyrics generally\n\nIs there a lastfm scrobble feature?\nNo, and not planned use PanoScrobbler https://github.com/kawaiiDango/pano-scrobbler. works with any player and has lots of features\nIs there a discord rich presence feature (RPC)?\nNo, and not planned use:\n\nKizzy on android https://github.com/dead8309/Kizzy\nmusic presence on desktop https://github.com/ungive/discord-music-presence\nthey work with any player\n\nEqualizer issues or missing feature\nnamida equalizer is simple and uses native android effects, always recommend using system wide eq apps for better experience and more features.\nmost extra features require writing custom audio engine or make sure every android version supports this effect, none of these are planned.\nif you have root you can use jamesdsp or viper4android.\notherwise use Equalizer314 or RootlessJamesDSP.\nSpotify Support\nNot planned.\nImporting spotify history was added recently in beta\nbut that’s all.\nReason is simply spotify is notorious for blocking any attempts at any unofficial clients. even if namida implements that, it will simply be hit by a dmca and no longer have support.\nWhat u can do as an alternative is convert ur spotify playlists to ytm, then login in namida to view ur yt playlists.\nwe barely keeping yt support alive as is.\nAlternatives: spotiflac or other tools like it\nSome FLAC files have no sound at some point\ncheck the source u got it from, try using ffmpeg with a compression level of 5 on the file\nffmpeg -y -i &quot;path/to/file.flac&quot; -map 0 -c:a flac -compression_level 5 -c:v copy &quot;path/to/output.flac&quot;\n\n"},"1":{"title":"FAQ > Frequently Asked Questions","id":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions","text":""},"2":{"title":"FAQ > Do I need to pay to use youtube?","id":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions-do-i-need-to-pay-to-use-youtube","text":""},"3":{"title":"FAQ > Slow/Broken yt loading/downloads","id":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions-slowbroken-yt-loadingdownloads","text":""},"4":{"title":"FAQ > Lyrics Source","id":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions-lyrics-source","text":""},"5":{"title":"FAQ > Change Lyrics Source","id":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions-change-lyrics-source","text":""},"6":{"title":"FAQ > Is there a lastfm scrobble feature?","id":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions-is-there-a-lastfm-scrobble-feature","text":""},"7":{"title":"FAQ > Is there a discord rich presence feature (RPC)?","id":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions-is-there-a-discord-rich-presence-feature-rpc","text":""},"8":{"title":"FAQ > Equalizer issues or missing feature","id":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions-equalizer-issues-or-missing-feature","text":""},"9":{"title":"FAQ > Spotify Support","id":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions-spotify-support","text":""},"10":{"title":"FAQ > Some FLAC files have no sound at some point","id":"faq/#frequently-asked-questions-some-flac-files-have-no-sound-at-some-point","text":""},"11":{"title":"Quick Start","id":"/","text":"Quick Start Your Docs 🚀\nThis is the home page of your new docmd project. You’re currently viewing docs/index.md — edit it, and your site updates.\nRun the dev server\nnpx @docmd/core dev\n\nOpen http://localhost:3000 — the page auto-reloads as you edit.\nBuild for production\nnpx @docmd/core build\n\nOutput goes to site/. Deploy that folder anywhere that serves static files.\nProject structure\n.\n├── docs/                  # Your markdown content\n│   └── index.md           # You are here\n├── assets/                # Custom CSS, JS, and images\n├── docmd.config.json      # Site configuration\n└── package.json           # Node dependencies + scripts\n\nFeatures\n1. Smart containers\n::: callout tip &quot;Did you know?&quot;\nYou can nest containers, add titles, and use icons.\n:::\n\n::: card &quot;Flexible&quot; icon:layout-grid\nOrganise content with cards.\n\n[View the docs →](https://docs.docmd.io){.docmd-button}\n:::\n\nRenders as a styled callout and a card with a button.\n2. Tabs and code\n::: tabs\n== tab &quot;JavaScript&quot; icon:braces\n```javascript\nconsole.log(&#039;Hello World&#039;);\n```\n\n== tab &quot;Python&quot; icon:code\n```python\nprint(&#039;Hello World&#039;)\n```\n:::\n\n3. Built-in plugins\ndocmd ships with these plugins enabled by default — no install needed:\n\nAI Assistant — interactive documentation chat (100% free with BYOK or docmd Cloud)\nSearch — full-text + semantic search (optional)\nSitemap + SEO meta tags\nLLMs context — llms.txt and llms.json for AI agents\nOKF — Open Knowledge Format bundle at site/okf/\nMermaid diagrams\nGit last-modified timestamps\nMath (KaTeX) — enable with docmd add math\n\nSee the full plugin list.\nNext steps\n\nInstall docmd\nConfigure your site\nBrowse templates\nDeploy to production\nGitHub repo\n\nHappy documenting! 🎉\n"},"12":{"title":"Quick Start > Quick Start Your Docs 🚀","id":"/#quick-start-your-docs","text":""},"13":{"title":"Quick Start > Run the dev server","id":"/#quick-start-your-docs-run-the-dev-server","text":""},"14":{"title":"Quick Start > Build for production","id":"/#quick-start-your-docs-build-for-production","text":""},"15":{"title":"Quick Start > Project structure","id":"/#quick-start-your-docs-project-structure","text":""},"16":{"title":"Quick Start > Features","id":"/#quick-start-your-docs-features","text":""},"17":{"title":"Quick Start > 1. Smart containers","id":"/#quick-start-your-docs-features-1-smart-containers","text":""},"18":{"title":"Quick Start > 2. Tabs and code","id":"/#quick-start-your-docs-features-2-tabs-and-code","text":""},"19":{"title":"Quick Start > 3. Built-in plugins","id":"/#quick-start-your-docs-features-3-built-in-plugins","text":""},"20":{"title":"Quick Start > Next steps","id":"/#quick-start-your-docs-next-steps","text":""},"21":{"title":"Theme Settings","id":"settings/1-theme-settings/","text":"\nTheme mode\nAuto coloring\n\n"},"22":{"title":"Indexer Settings","id":"settings/2-indexer-settings/","text":""},"23":{"title":"Settings","id":"settings/","text":"Settings\n\n\n  \n  \n  \n\nNote\nSome settings are only available for specific platforms or different android versions\n\n\nPress search icon in namida to easily find the setting you want.\n\n"},"24":{"title":"Settings > Settings","id":"settings/#settings","text":""},"25":{"title":"Agent Skills","id":"skills/","text":"Agent Skills\ndocmd ships a modular skill set for AI coding agents (Claude Code, Cursor, Windsurf, Copilot, etc.). The skills teach your agent the docmd CLI, configuration, plugin system, and the docmd mcp server — so it can build, configure, validate, and deploy sites for you.\nWhat gets installed\nThe docmd-skills npm package contains three skill modules:\n\n\n\nSkill\nWhen your agent loads it\n\n\n\n\ndocmd-skills\nA docmd site operator. Knows the npx @docmd/core CLI, docmd.config.json, plugins, themes, deployment, and the docmd mcp server.\n\n\ndocmd-dev\nA docmd framework contributor. Knows the monorepo layout, how to author plugins and templates, the JS / Rust engine loaders, and the public Node API (EngineLoader, createActionDispatcher, TemplateSlot).\n\n\ndocmd-writer\nA multi-language documentation writer. Drafts and reviews prose in any language, with SEO awareness and docmd’s markdown conventions (containers, frontmatter, file-title rule).\n\n\n\nInstall\nPick the directory your agent reads skills from and run one command:\nClaude Code\nnpx docmd-skills ~/.claude/skills\n\nCursor\nnpx docmd-skills ~/.cursor/skills\n\nProject-local (any agent)\nnpx docmd-skills ./.skills\n\nAfter install, the docmd-skills, docmd-dev, and docmd-writer modules are available to your agent.\nRun npx docmd-skills --help for the full list of commands.\nHow it works at runtime\nOnce installed, your agent automatically loads the right skill based on the files in scope:\n\nWhen you ask “add a plugin to my docmd site” → docmd-skills loads\nWhen you ask “add a new template” inside the cloned docmd-io/docmd monorepo → docmd-dev loads\nWhen you ask “write the intro for my new docs” → docmd-writer loads\n\nUpdate or remove\nThe CLI is idempotent — running it again updates the skills to latest:\nnpx docmd-skills &lt;dir&gt;          # updates all three\nnpx docmd-skills remove &lt;dir&gt;   # deletes all three\n\n"},"26":{"title":"Agent Skills > Agent Skills","id":"skills/#agent-skills","text":""},"27":{"title":"Agent Skills > What gets installed","id":"skills/#agent-skills-what-gets-installed","text":""},"28":{"title":"Agent Skills > Install","id":"skills/#agent-skills-install","text":""},"29":{"title":"Agent Skills > Claude Code","id":"skills/#agent-skills-install-claude-code","text":""},"30":{"title":"Agent Skills > Cursor","id":"skills/#agent-skills-install-cursor","text":""},"31":{"title":"Agent Skills > Project-local (any agent)","id":"skills/#agent-skills-install-project-local-any-agent","text":""},"32":{"title":"Agent Skills > How it works at runtime","id":"skills/#agent-skills-how-it-works-at-runtime","text":""},"33":{"title":"Agent Skills > Update or remove","id":"skills/#agent-skills-update-or-remove","text":""}},"dirtCount":0,"index":[["~",{"2":{"25":2}}],["🎉",{"2":{"11":1}}],["```python",{"2":{"11":1}}],["```",{"2":{"11":2}}],["```javascript",{"2":{"11":1}}],["==",{"2":{"11":2}}],["→",{"2":{"11":1,"25":3}}],["+",{"2":{"11":3}}],["└──",{"2":{"11":2}}],["│",{"2":{"11":1}}],["├──",{"2":{"11":3}}],["3000",{"2":{"11":1}}],["3",{"0":{"19":1},"1":{"11":1,"19":1},"2":{"11":1}}],["2",{"0":{"18":1},"1":{"11":1,"18":1},"2":{"11":1}}],["100",{"2":{"11":1}}],["1",{"0":{"17":1},"1":{"11":1,"17":1},"2":{"11":1}}],["112913142",{"2":{"0":1}}],["🚀",{"0":{"12":1},"1":{"11":1,"12":1},"2":{"11":1}}],[">",{"0":{"1":1,"2":1,"3":1,"4":1,"5":1,"6":1,"7":1,"8":1,"9":1,"10":1,"12":1,"13":1,"14":1,"15":1,"16":1,"17":1,"18":1,"19":1,"20":1,"24":1,"26":1,"27":1,"28":1,"29":1,"30":1,"31":1,"32":1,"33":1}}],["039",{"2":{"11":4}}],["0",{"2":{"0":1}}],["quick",{"0":{"11":1,"12":2,"13":1,"14":1,"15":1,"16":1,"17":1,"18":1,"19":1,"20":1},"1":{"11":1,"12":1},"2":{"11":1}}],["quot",{"2":{"0":4,"11":8}}],["questions",{"0":{"1":1},"1":{"0":1,"1":1},"2":{"0":1}}],["5",{"2":{"0":2}}],["javascript",{"2":{"11":1}}],["jamesdsp",{"2":{"0":1}}],["json",{"2":{"11":3,"25":1}}],["js",{"2":{"11":1,"25":1}}],["just",{"2":{"0"